# Committed, non-secret production defaults.
#
# Read this before adding anything here.
#
# Next.js loads this file for production builds AND in the production runtime,
# and a value present here can win over the one configured in Vercel. That makes
# it the wrong place for a placeholder.
#
# This file used to carry placeholder database, NextAuth, Google OAuth and
# Nutrient credentials, added to avoid "Invalid URL" errors during builds. The
# database ones broke production: lib/prisma.ts prefers
# DATABASE_POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL, saw the localhost placeholder, took the branch
# that skips the Neon driver adapter, and every query then tried 127.0.0.1:5432.
# The real Neon URL was configured in Vercel the whole time and never got used.
#
# The placeholders were also unnecessary. lib/prisma.ts builds its client lazily
# through a Proxy, so nothing connects to a database during the build.
#
# Rule: only add a value here if it is not a secret AND it is correct in
# production. Anything else belongs in Vercel's environment settings alone.

# Nutrient Viewer CDN version. Not a secret, and this is the real value, so it is
# safe for it to win. Loaded by app/layout.tsx from
# https://cdn.cloud.pspdfkit.com/pspdfkit-web@<version>/nutrient-viewer.js
NUTRIENT_VIEWER_VERSION="1.20.0"
